 the comics supposed to do a  smaller film with a 35 million dollar  budget and make it a hard-r which sounds  pretty awesome for a movie about an  occult detective fresh thinking  unfortunately the suits didn't find it  as interesting as lawrence and the  studio passed maybe it was all just a  test it's only in the face of horror  that you truly find you'll notice l.a  Constantine TV show flopped after plan  to the sequel went nowhere Warner  Brothers decided to go a different  direction with the property result a  Constantine TV series which debuted on  NBC in 2014  starring matt ryan the show took a  somewhat more faithful approach to the  character but it was still cancelled  after just 13 episodes the character has  since appeared in a guest role on the  CW's arrow so even though the show is no  longer around the existence of a  competing version of the properties film  muddies the waters for any possible film  sequel it may be rebooted one of the  most exciting projects in the DC  Cinematic Universe is the proposed  Justice League dark movie which features  John Constantine as part of a group of  supernatural types who tackle mystical  threats the regular Justice League isn't  equipped to handle that opens a big can  of worms in terms of Constantine - sure  Reeves might be up for a sequel but what  he wanted to play the character is part  of an ensemble superhero movie if not  it's very possible the character will be  recast making a reboot more likely than  the sequel sure Constantine was able to  defeat Satan but there's one thing even  he can't beat Hollywood  thanks for watching click the looper  icon subscribe to our YouTube channel  plus check out all this cool stuff we  know you'll love to  [Music]
 

